Calibration of the noise scale (sigma_eps^2 * Q):
  Pre-war:  sigma_eps^2 * Q = 2.99
  Post-war: sigma_eps^2 * Q = 6.24

======================================================================
MINIMUM DETECTABLE DECAY TIME (95% confidence, exact form)
======================================================================

  Pre-war 1820-1913:
    Q1 threshold (1 - 1/(3 T_max))   = 0.9894
    Estimated SE on |hat lambda|      = 0.0064
    2 * SE                            = 0.0128
    1 / (3 * T_max)                   = 0.0106
    Margin (1/(3*T_max) - 2*SE) = -0.0022 <= 0
    Interpretation: the noise floor exceeds the Q1 threshold's
    distance from unit modulus. Even genuinely neutral modes
    (|lambda| = 1) cannot be reliably distinguished from
    sub-threshold modes given the available precision.
    The Q1 test has effectively zero power on this sub-window.

  Post-war 1945-2020:
    Q1 threshold (1 - 1/(3 T_max))   = 0.9868
    Estimated SE on |hat lambda|      = 0.0297
    2 * SE                            = 0.0594
    1 / (3 * T_max)                   = 0.0132
    Margin (1/(3*T_max) - 2*SE) = -0.0462 <= 0
    Interpretation: the noise floor exceeds the Q1 threshold's
    distance from unit modulus. Even genuinely neutral modes
    (|lambda| = 1) cannot be reliably distinguished from
    sub-threshold modes given the available precision.
    The Q1 test has effectively zero power on this sub-window.

======================================================================
WHAT N_eff WOULD BE REQUIRED FOR ADEQUATE POWER?
======================================================================

To detect a mode with decay time tau_target, the test needs:
    SE on |hat lambda| <= [1/(3 T_max) - 1/tau_target] / 2

Assuming sigma_eps^2 * Q (the calibrated noise scale) is constant:

  Pre-war 1820-1913 (current N_eff = 467):
    decay tau = 100y: needs N_eff >= 9365 (20.1x current)
    decay tau = 150y: needs N_eff >= 1505 (3.2x current)
    decay tau = 200y: needs N_eff >= 1060 (2.3x current)

  Post-war 1945-2020 (current N_eff = 210):
    decay tau = 100y: needs N_eff >= 3950 (18.8x current)
    decay tau = 150y: needs N_eff >= 1922 (9.2x current)
    decay tau = 200y: needs N_eff >= 1529 (7.3x current)

